{
  "tema": 7259,
  "slug": "no-verdad-coletillas",
  "titulo": "Question tags: ¿no? and ¿verdad?",
  "subtitulo": "«Eres de Tijuana, ¿verdad?»",
  "foto": "t03.jpg",
  "regla": "To turn a statement into a check like _isn't it?_ or _right?_, add **¿no?** or **¿verdad?** at the end. They never change. After a negative statement, use only **¿verdad?**",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English builds a tag from the verb: _isn't it?_, _don't you?_, _didn't he?_. Spanish is much easier: one **fixed** tag for everything."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "statement",
            ", +",
            "¿no? / ¿verdad?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**¿no?** and **¿verdad?** mean the same with an affirmative statement: you expect a _yes_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "After a **negative** statement, use **¿verdad?**, not **¿no?**: **No vienes, ¿verdad?**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Write a **comma** before the tag, and put the **¿ ?** only around the tag."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In Mexico you'll also hear **¿o no?** (a bit pushier) and **¿cierto?** They work like **¿no?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Eres de Tijuana, ==¿verdad?==",
              "en": "You're from Tijuana, aren't you?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Hace calor, ==¿no?==",
              "en": "It's hot, isn't it?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mañana hay buenas olas, ==¿no?==",
              "en": "There are good waves tomorrow, right?"
            },
            {
              "es": "No te gusta el cilantro, ==¿verdad?==",
              "en": "You don't like cilantro, do you?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Ustedes ya comieron, ==¿verdad?==",
              "en": "You've already eaten, haven't you?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Ella entrena jiu-jitsu, ==¿no?==",
              "en": "She trains jiu-jitsu, doesn't she?"
            },
            {
              "es": "No hay tráfico en la garita, ==¿verdad?==",
              "en": "There's no traffic at the border crossing, is there?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Está padre la película, ==¿o no?==",
              "en": "The movie is great, isn't it?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "No tienes hambre, ¿no?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "No tienes hambre, ¿verdad?"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "After a negative: ¿verdad?"
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "¿Hace frío, no?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Hace frío, ¿no?"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "The question marks go only around the tag."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Eres mexicano, ¿no eres?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Eres mexicano, ¿no?"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "The tag never repeats the verb."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Vienes mañana ¿verdad?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Vienes mañana, ¿verdad?"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Comma before the tag."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
